             $VER: FPNLDownload, v1.00 (30-Jun-96) by Dotoran!
-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

Disclaimer:
~~~~~~~~~~
    Originally, v.40 was written by PMK, aka Peter Klein. Since Peter has
decided to go the IBM route, I'll be attempting to "take on" the continued
development of the files he has authored in the past.

What Is It:
~~~~~~~~~~
    This little file will scan your nodelist directory, then present the
user with a listing of the available NodeLists. They can then pick multiple
nodelists to download.

    Once chosen, the lists will be packed using the user's chosen packer,
as set in their accounts(or the file will be copied without packing, if the
user hasn't set a pack type(.TXT) yet).

    The SysOp also has the ability to specify certain NodeLists as being
PRIVATE, in which case they would NOT be shown to the user, and thus could
not be downloaded.

How To Install:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1. Copy the "FPNLD/" directory into your "FPFiles/" directory(if you have
   one presently). If not, then copy the "FPFiles/FPNLD/" directory anywhere
   on your system. All Dotoran released "FP" files will be housed in this
   "FPFiles/" directory, so try to keep them all together if at all possible.

2. Edit the variables found near the top of the listing. Separate multiple
   entries in the same variable with spaces. If running a CNet version in
   the 4.xx series(4.11 or later), set the "cnet" variable equal to "2",
   however if using v3.05c (or an early 4.xx), set "cnet" equal to "1".

3. Add the following line to your BBSMENU, Menu # 2; Available Everywhere:

            FPNLDownload    `28-    | {#0<path>FPFiles/FPNLD/FPNLD}
                            ^         ^
                      AccessGroups    Control-Q

   NOTE1: Make the Access Group range only those users you wish to give
          access to download the nodelists(usually just SysOps, eh?)

   NOTE2: Replace <path> with the path you used in step 1 above.

4. That's it! Reload BBSMENU, via clicking the Control Panel and pressing
   RAMIGA - T key combo(or use Text/Menu Reload from the CNet Menu).

                                                                - Dotoran
